<newsitem itemid="201065" id="root" date="1996-11-19" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: EMI H1 pre-tax, pre-excep profit up 9 pct.</title>
<headline>EMI H1 pre-tax, pre-excep profit up 9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		15.1		   vs 13.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  8.0		   vs 7.1</p>
<p> Pretax, pre-excep     112.5		   vs 102.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 90 to 120 million stg.  </p>
<p> Turnover		   1,468		  vs 1,445</p>
<p> Operating result	 119.8		  vs 115.6</p>
<p> Exceptional gain	  33.7		  vs 3.6</p>
<p> Finance charges	    7.3		  vs 12.8</p>
<p> Tax			   48.7		  vs 41.6</p>
<p> Net taxed		   97.5		  vs 64.8</p>
<p> Cost of minorities	 5.1		  vs 5.7</p>
<p> Attributable		92.4		  vs 59.1</p>
<p> Pay date		    March 7 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date   January 14, 1997</p>
<p> Ex-div date		 January 6, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - EMI, demerged from Thorn Plc in August, is one of the world's leading music companies. It said the exceptional gain was derived mainly from the sale of its stake in Thorn Securities.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
